<title>MEXICO: Mexico's crude port Dos Bocas reopened - port.</title>
<headline>Mexico's crude port Dos Bocas reopened - port.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's second largest crude port Dos Bocas in Tabasco state reopened at 0800 local/1600 GMT Monday as wind speeds relaxed to between 15 and 20 km per hour, a port official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The port had been shut since Saturday. Other crude port Pajaritos in Veracruz state remained shut, and Cayo Arcas in Campeche state remained open over the weekend as a cold front descended on the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
